<% layout('layout') %>
<% const legal = it.legal || {}; %>
<main class="sf-legal-page">
  <div class="sf-legal-container">
    <nav class="sf-legal-breadcrumb"><a href="/">← Back to SuggFeed</a></nav>
    <header class="sf-legal-header"><h1>Terms of Service</h1><p class="sf-legal-meta">Updated: 15 October 2026</p></header>
    <article class="sf-legal-content">
      <section><h2>About the service</h2>
        <% if (legal.operatorName) { %><p>Service operator: <%= legal.operatorName %>.</p><% } %>
        <% if (!legal.operatorName || !legal.privacyEmail) { %><p><strong>Operator details are incomplete.</strong> This deployment has not completed its school-use setup.</p><% } %>
        <p>SuggFeed provides feedback, discussion, moderation and progress tracking. Schools must authorize their participation and establish applicable policies before using it for school records. A platform account does not by itself establish school membership or staff authority.</p>
      </section>
      <section><h2>Accounts and participation</h2><p>Students and authorized staff may use accounts. Anonymous feedback is available where supported. Protect your credentials and private tracking codes. Eligibility, minors' participation and school responsibilities require the adopting school's approved process. This service is not an emergency response or formal confidential case-management system.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Acceptable use</h2><ul>
        <li>Do not threaten, harass, impersonate others or submit unlawful content.</li>
        <li>Do not publish another person's private information or sexual/abusive material.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt unauthorized access, bypass permissions, identify anonymous authors or interfere with service availability.</li>
        <li>Do not spam, manipulate votes or knowingly submit deceptive reports.</li>
      </ul><p>Good-faith criticism and safety concerns should be handled fairly. Use the school's designated confidential reporting route for sensitive allegations; avoid identifying people in public ideas.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Content and moderation</h2><p>You retain rights you hold in your content and permit the operator to process and display it as needed to provide the requested service, subject to applicable law and the Privacy Notice. Do not upload content you have no right to share. Approved ideas and public discussions or progress evidence may be visible beyond your school.</p><p>Authorized moderators may review, restrict or remove content under applicable policies. You may report content through the available reporting controls; ask the responsible operator about a moderation decision or an accessible reporting alternative. Anonymous mode does not guarantee untraceability.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Privacy and your rights</h2><p>Read the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a> for data categories, visibility, storage and contact details. These terms do not waive statutory privacy rights or replace a school's lawful-basis assessment, processing agreement or safeguarding obligations.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Availability and changes</h2><p>The service may be interrupted for maintenance, incidents or provider outages. Submission does not guarantee that an idea will be accepted or completed. Applicable statutory rights remain in force. School service commitments, support arrangements and termination/data-return requirements must be agreed separately with the operator.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Contact</h2>
        <% if (legal.privacyEmail) { %><p>Privacy requests: <a href="mailto:<%= legal.privacyEmail %>"><%= legal.privacyEmail %></a>. For school decisions, contact the school's authorized office.</p><% } else { %><p>The operator must provide monitored privacy and support contacts before school deployment. Do not send requests to an assumed SuggFeed email address.</p><% } %>
      </section>
    </article>
    <footer class="sf-legal-footer"><a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a><a href="/">Home</a></footer>
  </div>
</main>
